+# Root development-context continuation plan
+
+Scope: execute the owner's 2026-11-10 continuous mission directive using the
+EXISTING MissionController/Journal. No second controller, scheduler, ledger,
+authority, retry executor, service, background loop or deployment is introduced.
+Directive raw SHA256: e4d3ba8e181a3297b031e3438ab56625751ea4c6d224158c61087e28f8f364ee.
+
+1. Preserve all v1 task APIs/receipts; append closed development-continuation/v2
+   observations in the same marker-v2 local journal. Bind exact task snapshots,
+   retain sticky stale history throughA-B-A, fixed retry maximum/nondecreasing
+   usage, global sequence CAS and existing byte/record limits.
+2. Preserve prior40 Mission tests and add10 regressions; all50 must execute through
+   module/discovery. Move direct-file main guard to EOF. Preserve all122 prior
+   Supervisor cases and register the10 additional cases, giving132. No skip,
+   expected-failure substitution or selection narrowing is permitted.
+3. Qualify exact integrated source using safe owned unit/SQLite cases only.
+   Separate Python-process restart receipts from any actual Codex app restart.
+4. Only after source review/local qualification and a Draft PR, initialize ONE
+   private development journal at
+   C:/Users/LS-5/.codex/unified-master-mission/mission.db if absent. Existing files
+   are never deleted/adopted/repaired implicitly. No ACL/account/policy changes.
+5. Archive eight owners' handoff snapshots through existing v1 task/evidence
+   APIs with exact raw digests and lossless bounded encoded data. These are
+   UNTRUSTED_OBSERVATIONS: owner claims/dependency descriptors/status layers are
+   retained, not converted to native grants, executable DAG or accepted runtime.
+   Archive tasks are independent context-intake tasks, not replacement tasks
+   for authority/Scheduler/Storage. Preserve original raw identities and scopes.
+6. Add an explicit Root read-only CI-observation task with source/head/tree,
+   next step, evidence, retry budget and all required blockers/authorizations.
+   A fresh Python invocation reads its checkpoint; Root performs that one
+   allowlisted GitHub GET with existing tools, saves original evidence, then
+   appends an explicit completion checkpoint. Never execute arbitrary stored
+   descriptions or automatically retry workflows.
+7. Retain a private restoration packet with exact qualified engine source,
+   journal path/sequence/hash and safe read-only inspection instructions.
+   Metadata references confer no permissions. A later Codex session must verify
+   source and replay the journal before choosing a permitted action.
+8. CODEX_APP_RESTART_RECOVERY remains NOT_TESTED until the owner actually
+   restarts Codex and the restored agent proves a new safe action from that
+   journal. Python restart is a narrower result; no autonomous-dispatch claim.
+
+Validation focus: v1 compatibility; any-field/ABA sticky stale; CAS before
+idempotence; full historical retry bounds; byte/capacity/corrupt receipt rejection;
+deep detached observations; all native/runtime/physical/trading grants false;
+no raw handoff instruction execution or inferred owner approval.
+
+Milestone1 LS5 scoped pilot is retained without repeat. Milestone2 actual native
+Authority/Scheduler/resource-bound worker/committed Storage/authenticated Terminan
+remains unadmitted. Strict D4/logical DISABLED/public DENY, Math consumed single-use,
+PC4 existing-channel+separate-artifact block, ADMINIT exclusion, real orders and
